================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS FILE
================================================================================

  Plain text, append-only, in execution order. Every step is a command line
  introduced by '$ ', followed by its captured streams and its exit status:

      [stdout]  ... verbatim; nothing follows the marker when the stream was empty
      [stderr]  ... verbatim; java and the pre-touch proof write here, not to stdout
      [exit]    ... the command's exit status, then the UTC time it started and
                    the seconds it took

  Every table below is the verbatim stdout of the command shown immediately
  above it, so no figure in this file is transcribed from a table into prose.
  Commands that read a file print the fields they read; commands that count
  print the count. Nothing is reflowed or elided.

  The precondition and target-surface commands were run with harness/env.sh
  sourced in a fresh shell from the repository root, which is how every runner in
  this harness is invoked. The invocation itself was run from this clone's own
  scratch directory rather than from the repository, because joern eagerly
  creates an ~800 MB ./workspace in whatever directory it starts from; PHASE 3
  names that directory.

  Elapsed times are facts, not budgets. No time limit applies anywhere in this
  run, and none was imposed on this invocation.

  Where a figure did not come from a command in this file, it carries a
  provenance line naming the file it was read out of. PHASE 4 is entirely of
  that kind and says so at its head.

================================================================================
METHOD - THE FOUR PRINCIPLES THIS FILE IS HELD TO
================================================================================

  review_rules returned exactly 'No user rules provided.' for the whole
  document. That is a complete read, corroborated by AAP 0.7 and 0.10.2. NO
  USER-SPECIFIED RULE GOVERNS THIS FILE, and that absence is not read as licence
  to lower the bar; enterprise best practice is substituted, held to the AAP's
  own four principles.

  P1 Verification is independent of the thing verified. The graph's identity is
  recomputed from the bytes on disk before this query loads it - PHASE 1 STEP 2
  measures it with the shell, STEP 3 measures it again with an independent
  reader, and the query measured it a third time inside its own process - rather
  than being inherited from the frontend log or from the earlier stages that
  also loaded a graph at this path. The provenance of the difference in STEP 4
  comes from files this query does not write and did not read. And the
  duplicate-formulation question in PHASE 5 is ANSWERED BY ANALYSIS of both
  query sources, computed here, rather than taken from either query's own claim
  about itself.

  P2 Reject rather than infer. Whether the traversal bound was reached is
  reported AS MEASURED. This invocation did not reach the traversal at all, so
  it reports no bound-reached flag of its own and says so; the flag the earlier
  invocation measured is reproduced under its own provenance header, with the
  basis on which that invocation established it. Nothing is inferred from a
  result that came back, because none did.

  P3 Halt-and-report over silent repair. A graph-identity mismatch halts. It
  mismatched, the query halted, and this file reports it in the STATUS block
  above rather than working around it. A wrong JVM major halts; the major was
  measured twice and it is 21. A heap below the floor halts; the heap the query
  ACTUALLY received was measured inside the query's own process and it is exactly
  the floor. Nothing was retried, re-pointed at another record, or re-run with a
  loosened check to obtain a completed run.

  P4 Verbatim preservation. The console output is retained as emitted, complete,
  in APPENDIX A, and the file the query itself wrote at this path before it
  re-raised is retained complete in APPENDIX B, each with its byte size and
  sha256 so the copy can be checked against the source.

  NEVER FABRICATE A MEASUREMENT. Every number in this file either sits under a
  command that produced it or carries a provenance line naming the file it was
  read from. There is no third category.

================================================================================
VERDICT VOCABULARY
================================================================================

  PASS                : the condition was measured here and it holds.
  RECORDED DIFFERENCE : observed differs from expected; both values are recorded
                        and the run continues.
  OUTSTANDING         : a cross-check that cannot be performed yet because the
                        file that owns the other side does not exist on this
                        branch. Named, never assumed to agree.
  HALT-CLASS FINDING  : a condition AAP 0.9.2 treats as halting. ONE arose in
                        this invocation - the graph-identity mismatch - and the
                        query stopped on it. It is stated in the STATUS block,
                        measured in PHASE 1 STEP 3 and given its provenance in
                        STEP 4.
  NOT MEASURED HERE   : a figure this invocation could not take. Named, and
                        where the run's record carries the earlier invocation's
                        value it is reproduced with its provenance rather than
                        presented as this invocation's.

================================================================================
PHASE 1 - THE PRECONDITIONS THAT HAD TO HOLD BEFORE THE QUERY LOADED THE GRAPH
================================================================================

  Six preconditions, each a halt if it fails. The graph must be the graph the
  record describes. The load mechanism must be importCpg, and the alternative
  must not appear even textually in the committed query source. The JVM must
  report major 21. The heap the query actually receives must be at or above the
  64 GiB floor, and the host must be shown to COMMIT that heap rather than
  merely reserve it. Nothing else may hold a 64 GB Joern process at the same
  time. And the setup-time smoke override must be unset.

  FIVE OF THE SIX PASS. The first one - the graph is the graph the record
  describes - FAILS, and it is the halt this file is mostly about. The other
  five are still measured and reported, because a halt on one condition is not a
  licence to leave the rest unchecked: a reader has to be able to tell that the
  heap, the JDK, the loader and the sequencing were all in order and that the
  identity was the single thing wrong.

