================================================================================
PHASE 8 - THIS FILE, AND WHERE ITS OWN IDENTITY IS RECORDED
================================================================================

  8.1 THE TWO WRITES TO THIS PATH, both preserved

    The query resolves this path itself, in stage A, before any check that can
    stop the run - which is precisely why a halt leaves its console record on
    disk rather than only on a terminal. It wrote its accumulated console lines
    here from its catch block, after printing ---BLITZY-FAILURE--- and before
    re-raising. That file - 31 lines, 2545 bytes, sha256 cb682459...9dfe4 - was
    captured before this record was assembled and is reproduced COMPLETE and
    VERBATIM in APPENDIX B. This record then supersedes it at the same path,
    carrying it inside itself along with the full terminal transcript, of which
    it is a subset.

    Nothing is lost by that: APPENDIX A is the terminal transcript, which is a
    superset of APPENDIX B, and each appendix states its own byte size and sha256
    so either copy can be checked against the source.

  8.2 THIS FILE'S BYTE SIZE AND SHA256

    Owned by oss-scan-results/run-record.md, which holds the manifest of both
    artifact trees with a byte size and a sha256 per file, this one included.
    They are deliberately NOT written here: a digest of a file cannot appear
    inside that file, since writing it changes the bytes it describes. The
    manifest owner measures this file after it is closed, which is why the
    measurement lives there and is referenced from here.

    Both artifact trees are excluded from git's ordinary collection by
    .gitignore:31 (artifacts/), which is why publication is by that manifest and
    why this file is added explicitly rather than picked up by a plain add.

  8.3 WHAT THIS INVOCATION LEFT BEHIND, and why it stays

    Almost nothing, because the halt preceded every stage that writes. The
    query's own workspace at queries/joern/.workspace was never created beyond
    the .gitignore that was already there - joern's own ./workspace went to
    /tmp/blitzy-harness-scratch/1/probe-02/run, outside the repository, which is
    why the invocation was started from there. The captured streams and the
    capture harness stay in that same private scratch directory. Nothing is torn
    down, purged or reset: no cleanup, no temp purging, and what the run built
    stays where it is.

  8.4 THE ONE THING A READER SHOULD TAKE FROM THIS FILE

    The guard worked. A shared, provisioned input was replaced between lanes of
    one run, and the stage that would have consumed it detected the replacement
    from the bytes themselves and stopped instead of quietly producing figures
    about a graph nobody has. Everything else here - the runtime measurements,
    the target surface at the pin, the duplicate-formulation verdict, the
    selectors - is evidence taken around that halt rather than in spite of it,
    and every figure this invocation could not take is named as such.

